Subject: quartz: read hooked files synchronously, and VMR7 GetNativeVideoSize without a connection
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Modification date: 2026-11-22

From the quartz-video branch of github:moeleak/wine (on Wine 11.18). Translation
patches that replace a game's video by hooking the file functions (White Album 2's
Chinese one, for one) report a size of 0 from GetFileSizeEx() and fail overlapped
reads, so the async reader read an empty stream: the fallback of
quartz-filesource-vfs-fallback.patch only took over when the overlapped open, read
or GetFileSizeEx() failed. The reader now opens the file without
FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED, gets its size with GetFileSize(), and reads it with
SetFilePointer() and synchronous ReadFile() calls under a lock, completing requests
synchronously. VMR7's windowless GetNativeVideoSize() returns VFW_E_NOT_CONNECTED
without a connection instead of crashing, as VMR9's already does here.

Commits, in order (moeleak/wine):
  85acca26a9 quartz: Don't crash in GetNativeVideoSize() when the renderer isn't connected. (backported)
  bb57ae7de5 quartz: Read files synchronously in the async reader. (backported)

